# PebbleAgent — Version Notes

> Last updated: 2026-10-23

## Platform

- Python WebSocket gateway (JSON-RPC 2.0) with 60+ methods: sessions, projects, files, permissions, memory, MCP, pricing, notes, assistant messages, exports
- Vue 3 + Pinia frontend, Tauri 2 desktop shell (frameless window, sidecar backend, packaging pipeline)
- Runtime data under `%USERPROFILE%\.pebble\` (override with `PEBBLE_HOME`); project-scoped files live in the active project directory
- Licensing: project is AGPL-3.0; third-party skills and the `hyperframes` npm dependency are attributed in `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` (HyperFrames, Copyright 2026 HeyGen, Inc., Apache-2.0 — six `skills/hyperframes-*` / `video-hyperframes` directories each carry the full license text)

## Agent runtime

- Streaming chat loop with tool orchestration: parallel read-only batches, serial side-effect batches, concurrency semaphore, cancellation; per-round usage accounting from the stream consumer's captured usage chunk
- Context assembly: system prompt + project path + user note + recalled experience entries + agent note + skills; token accounting via `context_compressor.estimate_tokens` (tiktoken with CN/EN ratio fallback)
- Stream-end detection: finish_reason recording, suspicious-end auto-retry (once per turn), graceful completion
- Experience ledger: rule-based turn observation (correction / constraint / preference / pitfall), FTS5 recall with tool, path, kind, confidence, recency and capped hit weighting, dedupe + supersede lifecycle within the same scope (global or the current project_id), per-agent notes (user and project scopes merged into the prompt); statement capped at 160 characters and rationale at 300 on write, single entry capped at 240 characters on render; SQLite at `{PEBBLE_HOME:-~/.pebble}/experience.db`; agent-facing `experience_write` (kind / scope / keywords) and `experience_update` (id / statement / kind / rationale / confidence; scope fixed) tools
- Compaction summary: stable five-section handoff format (任务 / 现状 / 决定 / 待办 / 线索), single-pass prompt with no tool calls, format validation with one strict retry and a wrapped fallback; manual compaction keeps the newest 2 messages (at least 1) in both sessions.db and agent_chat.db
- Agent prompts: comment hygiene (no dates, no change / incident / refactor notes) and CKB document positioning (present-tense facts, no change narratives)
- Agent prompt governance: `code_agent_prompt.md` carries the CKB mechanism, the tool restriction order (last-resort `powershell` / `execute_code` gated on three sufficiency conditions), language policy (reply in the user's language), the `[MUST]` severity suffix on 13 headings (no `(must)` / `(mandatory rule)` / `(important!)` / `(violation = failure)` variants), CKB build exemptions (user override / read-only question / damaged knowledge base), the MCP-unavailable CKB fallback, the compile-based LSP fallback, and retry backoff with a 60s budget; `tests/test_code_agent_prompt_contract.py` holds prompt tool names, the YAML allowlist, the severity wording, and the language policy in sync
- Turn building blocks: `agent_core/chat/usage.py` (pricing, per-call cost, session accumulation), `chat/prompt.py` (system prompt composition), `chat/stream_client.py` (streamed request, retries, context-window handling, chunk accumulation), `chat/tool_cycle.py` (question injection, tool execution, result write-back), `chat/turn_executor.py` (turn preparation: agent, conversation, user message, history, prompt, client, cancel signal)
- Session persistence: dual-DB (sessions.db for UI state, agent_chat.db for LLM context), transcript JSONL, message-chain tracking

## Agents

- `chat_agent` — daily chat; `enforce=true` allowlist of 32 entries: read_file / search_files / search_in_file / grep / glob, web_search / fetch_url / browser_navigate, 14 read-only GitHub MCP methods, 10 read-only Chrome DevTools MCP methods (schema filtering + execution-entry interception; writes, exec, downloads, clarify and tool-discovery are denied)
- `code_agent` — full toolset via `enforce=true` with an empty allowlist (empty means no filtering, so every tool including newly installed ones is granted); restriction is delegated entirely to the permission chain; CKB preloaded, system prompt in `agent_core/agents/code_agent_prompt.md`
- YAML-defined: tools permission, behavior, skills preload, system prompt (inline or file)

## Tools

- 53 built-in tools across file, shell, network, media, memory, planning, UI, and utility groups; MCP proxy tools (`mcp__*`); schema and `TOOL_HANDLERS` are in one-to-one correspondence (53 / 53), including `web_search`, which fetches `cn.bing.com/search` over httpx, parses structured results and is rate-limited by little_guard
- Interaction tools: `clarify` (structured questions: title / prompt / options label+detail / multiple), `todo_write` / `todo_read` (session checklist), `enter_plan_mode` / `exit_plan_mode` / `create_plan` / `get_plan`
- Dispatch: one declarative registry (`agent_core/tool_impl/registry.py`) maps tool names to handlers; handlers live in per-domain modules (filesystem / execution / web / documents / system / workspace / lsp / mcp_bridge); `tool_executor_impl.py` is the execution pipeline facade (policy → permission → snapshot → dispatch → write-result backfill)
- Shell validation: BashValidator (read-only / destructive / mode / sed / path / semantic), PowerShellValidator (destructive patterns + path boundary), code destructive scan, per-tool runtime limits in `little_guard` (rate / navigation / download counters scoped per conversation via contextvar, reset per turn); network behaviour of `execute_code` and `powershell` is not content-scanned
- Permission chain: modes (manual / auto / readonly; readonly allows the READONLY_TOOLS allowlist — reads, git, env, LSP, todo/plan, plus web_search / fetch_url / browser_navigate, with browser_download and every write rejected; deny rules are evaluated before the readonly allowlist, and high-confidence secret reads (filename patterns plus secrets / credentials directory segments) are blocked in every mode — auto rejects, manual asks, readonly rejects, allow rules cannot bypass), allow / deny / ask rules with `tool:pattern` syntax, path whitelist, project boundary checks, per-(session, permission_type) trust, inline-code escalation, fail-closed on module errors
- Audit: permission decisions persisted with chained SHA256 checksum (v3) and write-time secret masking
- Snapshots: write-ahead file snapshots; single-file revert matches records by normalized absolute path, reverts one version per click and reports `remaining`; a failed restore leaves the record active; the RPC runs in the thread pool; external-modification detection; undo support

## Gateway

- WebSocket auth (token file + query parameter), Origin checks, payload limits, connection cap
- RPC dispatch: `gateway/rpc/` domain handlers (session, mcp, file, model, memory, permission, project, config, misc) behind a prefix router; `handle_request` builds an `RpcContext` and delegates
- `file.*` RPC family with project-boundary guard; `permission.*` family with sync evaluation; `session.*`, `project.*`, `memory.*`, `mcp.*`, `pricing.*`
- MCP lifecycle: auto-install (sha256-verified), project-level approval, background initialization, per-server runtime state; unconfigured optional servers render as Optional with a Set path hint instead of a hard error

## Frontend

- Streaming render pipeline: 120ms throttled refresh, line-level cache, compacted-message folding with divider + pill (`SegmentedMessageList.vue`, segments split by compaction boundaries)
- Styles: `styles/index.css` imports ten domain files in cascade order (base / layout / sidebar / messages / input / panels / widgets / cards / settings / overlays)
- Theme system: five built-in palettes plus custom colors; current theme, custom themes, and per-theme colors persist to `theme.json` through `theme.get` / `theme.save`; saving applies the color immediately and a save failure does not undo the applied theme
- Message flow: execution-order rendering (thinking / tool / question / content), inline clarify cards (title / prompt / options label+detail / multiple), multi-question answers, image attachments with viewer
- Compaction card: 任务 / 现状 / 决定 / 待办 / 线索 sections with counts
- HTML preview: sandboxed iframe (allow-scripts only), injected meta CSP, postMessage bridge, PNG capture, interactive comment layer
- Preview dock (`PreviewDock.vue` + `stores/preview.ts`): the only live preview iframe lives in a right-side dock, outside the message flow; every `@pebble-file` in the conversation is registered with tabs to switch between generated files, dock width/open state persist to localStorage, non-active files get a stale dot, a floating button reopens a closed dock; message flow renders `html-file` blocks as reference chips so two iframes never share the global comment store
- Config panels: LLM providers/models, thinking toggle and reasoning effort, price editor with hot reload, MCP panel, permission mode (three options: manual / auto / read-only; a mode the panel does not recognize is shown verbatim with an explicit warning instead of silently falling back to Manual)
- Permission dialog: blocking request queue (overlay clicks do not dismiss), per-request remember duration, Deny / Deny Current / Allow All
- Overlay guards: panels keep unsaved input (pricing warns once before discarding, path whitelist saves on close, rename / add-path / Set path inputs block outside dismissal)
- Reconnect recovery: disconnect detection, resume-based display restoration, short-poll for in-flight turns

